When window.stop() stops an object element’s fetch, Ladybird stops
delaying the load event on it, so the document’s readyState reaches
“complete”. Chrome 158 and Firefox 151 report “complete” right after
window.stop() too, and fire an error event at the object. WebKit 26.5
keeps “interactive”. None of the three fires a load event at the
window, while Ladybird fires one once nothing else delays it, as it
already did for an image whose fetch was stopped.
